-- title:
--   Eigenform realisation at primes of the integral Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ be an integer and suppose that $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ has an integral structure in the sense of [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6): the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule generated by those weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers is the whole space. Let $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 {ℓ | ℓ ∣ N}`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to the primes $\ell \nmid N$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to primes $q \mid N$ not in the excluded set (a vacuous family here, since the excluded set consists of all divisors of $N$); thus $\mathbb{T}$ is the anemic Hecke algebra $\mathbb{Z}[T_\ell : \ell \nmid N]$. Let $\mathfrak{p} \subset \mathbb{T}$ be a prime ideal such that the only integer $n$ whose image under $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{T}$ lies in $\mathfrak{p}$ is $n = 0$, i.e. $\mathfrak{p} \cap \mathbb{Z} = 0$. Then there exists $f \in S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ satisfying the relations of `IsNormalizedEigenform`, namely $a_1(f) = 1$, $a_{mn}(f) = a_m(f)a_n(f)$ for coprime $m,n$, and, for $p$ prime, $a_{p^{r+2}}(f) = a_p(f)a_{p^{r+1}}(f) - p\,a_{p^r}(f)$ when $p \nmid N$ and $a_{p^{r+2}}(f) = a_p(f)a_{p^{r+1}}(f)$ when $p \mid N$, such that every $t \in \mathbb{T}$ with $t f = 0$ lies in $\mathfrak{p}$.
--
--   This is the eigenform-realisation step: the annihilator in the integral Hecke algebra of a suitable normalised weight-$2$ eigenform is contained in any given prime of residue characteristic zero, in the style of the auxiliary lemmas of Deligne–Serre on weight-one forms. It is used in the Deligne–Serre style lifting statement [`CuspForm.exists_isNormalizedEigenform_congruent_of_isMaximal`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_isNormalizedEigenform_congruent_of_isMaximal) and in [`CuspForm.exists_isNewform_point_factor`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_isNewform_point_factor).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_isNormalizedEigenform_ker_le_of_isPrime.lean

